From: Local build <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] EXP: plasmawindowmanagement: send window geometry once per pass of the event loop (KWIN_PLASMA_WINDOW_GEOMETRY_COALESCE)

An interactive move changes a window's frame and client geometry at every pointer event, and each
change was sent at once as org_kde_plasma_window.geometry and client_geometry to every client of
Plasma window management. In plasmashell, libtaskmanager turns each event into a dataChanged that
runs through its proxy models into every task and pager delegate: with a 4000 Hz mouse, a guest's
plasmashell spent its main thread on that backlog and froze for 12 s after a fast drag
(2026-10-17).

The narrow alternative to moving the window once per frame (0060): only the broadcast is batched.
Each window keeps its latest geometry and client geometry and sends them on a zero timer, so all
the changes made in one pass of the event loop reach the clients as one event of each kind, in the
order they had before (client_geometry, then geometry). A client that binds in between still gets
the latest values in its initial state; an invalid geometry is still not sent.

This collapses the events that KWin handles in one pass: input that arrives in bursts (a VM's
virtual tablet, a nested compositor's socket) or a KWin that is busy and falls behind. A KWin that
handles each pointer event in a pass of its own still sends every geometry, and the move itself
(snap and confinement, scene items and repaints, effects) still happens at every event.

KWIN_PLASMA_WINDOW_GEOMETRY_COALESCE=0 sends every change at once, as before. See
findings/kwin-move-per-event-2026-10-17.md.


A host KWin keeps its wrapper's environment from login: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kwin-plasma-window-geometry-coalesce holding
0 or 1 overrides the variable while it exists, read at most once a second (an A/B in a running session).
---

diff --git a/src/wayland/plasmawindowmanagement.cpp b/src/wayland/plasmawindowmanagement.cpp
index ac4561c..3cb2523 100644
--- a/src/wayland/plasmawindowmanagement.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland/plasmawindowmanagement.cpp
@@ -16,8 +16,11 @@
 #include <QList>
 #include <QPointer>
 #include <QThreadPool>
+#include <QTimer>
 #include <QUuid>
 
+#include <chrono>
+
 #include <qwayland-server-plasma-window-management.h>
 
 #include <cerrno>
@@ -30,6 +33,30 @@ namespace KWin
 static const quint32 s_version = 21;
 static const quint32 s_activationVersion = 1;
 
+// KWIN_PLASMA_WINDOW_GEOMETRY_COALESCE=0 sends every geometry change at once: as before. A host KWin keeps its wrapper's environment from login, so
+// $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kwin-plasma-window-geometry-coalesce holding 0 or 1 decides instead while it exists, read at most once a second
+// (an A/B in a running session)
+static bool coalesceGeometries()
+{
+    static const bool s_environment = qEnvironmentVariable("KWIN_PLASMA_WINDOW_GEOMETRY_COALESCE") != QStringLiteral("0");
+    static const QString s_path = qEnvironmentVariable("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR") + QStringLiteral("/kwin-plasma-window-geometry-coalesce");
+    static bool s_value = s_environment;
+    static std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point s_lastRead;
+    const auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+    if (now - s_lastRead >= std::chrono::seconds(1)) {
+        s_lastRead = now;
+        s_value = s_environment;
+        QFile file(s_path);
+        if (file.open(QIODevice::ReadOnly)) {
+            const QByteArray value = file.readAll().trimmed();
+            if (value == "0" || value == "1") {
+                s_value = value == "1";
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    return s_value;
+}
+
 class PlasmaWindowManagementInterfacePrivate : public QtWaylandServer::org_kde_plasma_window_management
 {
 public:
@@ -82,6 +109,8 @@ public:
     void sendInitialState(Resource *resource);
     wl_resource *resourceForParent(PlasmaWindowInterface *parent, Resource *child) const;
     void setClientGeometry(const Rect &geometry);
+    void scheduleGeometries();
